B.Gk=new A.rT("01","Missing MFA","MFA",B.Fk,"Initial access","One stolen password was all it took.","Attackers signed in to a remote-access portal with stolen credentials. The portal asked for a password, but nothing else.","The remote-access portal only required a username and password.","A password stolen through phishing or reuse was enough to let an outsider into the network.","Require multi-factor authentication, ideally a phishing-resistant security key rather than a code that can be intercepted.")
B.Fh=new A.e1(63169,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Gj=new A.rT("02","Outdated Systems","Updates",B.Fh,"Known exploits","Old servers kept known flaws alive.","Once inside, the attackers found systems that had missed updates. Known flaws in that old software gave them a firmer foothold.","Old, unsupported software may stop receiving security updates.","Attackers could exploit published vulnerabilities that already had fixes available.","Test and install updates on a regular schedule, and replace systems that can no longer receive patches.")
B.Fl=new A.e1(983861,"MaterialIcons",!1)
B.Gi=new A.rT("03","Poor Network Separation","Network",B.Fl,"Lateral movement","A flat network let the breach spread.","Because the internal network was largely flat, the attackers could move from one system to another without meeting a real boundary.","Unnecessary connections can let an attacker reach other systems.","One infected device could lead to a much wider outage.","Separate important systems from each other and allow only the connections each one actually needs.")
